<!--Post: 7116--><!--Time: 1108190118-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7116"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:tbjostad@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Toto<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Toto<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 10:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey guys, great work, but before you go posting it everywhere, you need to this check out.   <BR> <BR>Go to the <b>GENERAL DISCUSSIONS</b> thread then <b>PUZZLES</b>.  Look for <b>Wichitaboy&#39;s 12/14/04</b> post.  He&#39;s got all the above &#40;and more&#41; plus links to pics of the puzzle as well.    <BR> <BR>Sorry IQ, great deductions though.  That&#39;s two great minds that have come to the same conclusion, think you guys hit the nail on the head!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7116-->
<!--Post: 7118--><!--Time: 1108191308-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7118"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 10:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Search this site &#34;grid&#34;. Very impressive, IQ &amp; Wichitaboy. My brain doesn&#39;t think that way.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7118-->
<!--Post: 7131--><!--Time: 1108221023-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7131"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In Wichitaboy&#39;s post, I didn&#39;t catch that the grid names MO, ID, RUSE were actually labeling the items beneath &amp; within its respective grid. <BR> <BR>&#40;Perhaps Wichitaboy was implying that, but I missed that particular aspect of it.&#41; <BR> <BR>IQ&#39;s post actually crystallized that for me. <BR> <BR>Great work -- both of you! <BR> <BR>Now, I guess we can connect each ruse to the murder?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7131-->
<!--Post: 7220--><!--Time: 1108294054-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7220"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:newmilleniumwriter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 3:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Too bad we don&#39;t have some brains like this on the PD.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7220-->
<!--Post: 7289--><!--Time: 1108367292-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7289"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 11:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I used the list of chapters from BTK&#39;s May letter as a key for a crossword puzzle. I answered his chapters putting the words vertically as in a crossword puzzle. For example, on #1 he had &#34;Serial Killer ____&#34;, so I answered &#34;story&#34;, and so on. I know, too much time in my hands. <BR> <BR>Anyway, at the end I ended up with garbage, but there were a few names in it. I am not implying that these people are BTK or have anything to do with BTK, just that the names showed on the puzzle thing. Since the names are so short it may also be coincidence that they showed. So, I ask whoever reads this post to not take it too seriously. <BR> <BR>1. Sam <BR>2. Sam A. <BR>3. Reyes <BR>4. Ines <BR>5. Iness <BR> <BR>Now Sama Reyes is supposedly a movie star, but I never heard of her before. I searched for the names in Wichita, but only found a few Reyeses who live around the area, nobody who would standout, though. I used <a href="http://www.switchboard.com" target=_top>http://www.switchboard.com</a> and <a href="http://www.searchbug.com" target=_top>http://www.searchbug.com</a> to search. <BR> <BR>While at it, I found out the name &#34;Ruse&#34; is really a last name, also the last name Kruse. Weird, huh?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7289-->
<!--Post: 7320--><!--Time: 1108400232-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7320"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 8:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since this thread is about MO-id ruse, maybe Chapter 7 is Fox and &#34;Chapter 8 MO-id ruse&#34; represents the time period between Fox and Wegerle. If BTK is writing a reference manual then things might be categorized and scattered around by subject &#40;i.e. &#34;Ruses&#34;&#41; and not relevant to time.  But if BTK is writing a story, chapters would be time relevent.  Just a thought on MO-id ruse.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7320-->
<!--Post: 7339--><!--Time: 1108408962-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7339"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tfoth <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t understand your theory. No offense, it may just be me, but I don&#39;t see how the chapter titled &#34;PJs&#34; is Fox &#40;as you said&#41;. I also don&#39;t understand how the word search could represent the time period between the two murders. Please elaborate. <BR> <BR>I do have another comment on the chapter list. In one of the communications, chapters 1,2 and 8 were missing from the list. Each chapter could be directly related to a communication BTK has sent the media and those chapters were excluded because they have already been given to them. <BR> <BR>For instance:  <BR> <BR>We&#39;ve established that chapter 8 is directly related to the word puzzle. What if the baby picture is an actual picture of BTK &#40;or another SERIAL KILLER&#41;. This communication could be chapter , A serial Killer _______ or it could refer to chapter 2, Dawn. <BR> <BR>This may be completely wrong, but I believe the MO-ID RUSE link suggests their may be a link between the communications and the chapter list. If we knew more about the communications it probably wouldn&#39;t be difficult at all. As someone on this site has suggested, LE has probably put these things together, then again maybe they have not. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>iq <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7339-->
<!--Post: 7350--><!--Time: 1108417892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7350"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 1:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IQ: You post great stuff. I have a reputation of being nuts so take that with a grain of salt.  I believe chapter 7 PJ&#39;s refers to Fox because it&#39;s nothing more than an old way of referencing pajamas which is a reference to what was left at the crime scene. I just can&#39;t connect the dots where it is a reference to PJ Wyatt at WSU because Oh Nancy sounds like a poem that was taught.... yadda yadda.. I just think it&#39;s a pajamas ref and chapter 7 is Fox/7th victim.   BTK &#34;disappeared&#34; after the Fox murder.  I think Chapter 8-MO-id Ruse most likely refers to what was going on during that time period between Fox and Wegerle so it deserves a chapter of its own. Again, chapters of a story would be in chronological order unless it was a reference book.  If it has been established that MO-id Ruse is somehow about puzzles, I am unaware of why. I think some puzzles accompanied a recent chapter list, but that&#39;s all I can see. I am the one that thinks BTK might be female so you might want to disregard my thoughts anyway. ;-&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7350-->
<!--Post: 7351--><!--Time: 1108418224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7351"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 1:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think he means Chapter 7 being Fox, as Fox being the 7th victim. Chapter 8 &#40;mo-id-ruse&#41; being a codeword for a date, like mm/dd/yyyy. <BR> <BR>I think the reasons why LE may be holding the communications are, because the letters are either too pornographic, too grotesque, or too threatening to the public. Look what the Otero letter had in it that police didn&#39;t want to make public. <BR> <BR>I hope they reconsider. Look how releasing Ted Kacksinski&#39;s manifesto do... someone recognized it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7351-->
<!--Post: 7353--><!--Time: 1108418819-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7353"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 2:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->7.PJ&#39;s=Fox <BR>8.MO-id ruse = Was using different MO and operating as a different id during the time period between Fox/Wegerle &#40;not &#34;BTK&#34; during this time&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7353-->
<!--Post: 7357--><!--Time: 1108422007-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7357"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tfoth &amp; Ztargate- I have to assume you haven&#39;t seen the word puzzle or read the original post in this thread because of your statement:  <BR> <BR>&#34;If it has been established that MO-idRuse is somehow about puzzles, I am unaware of why&#34; <BR> <BR>Let&#39;s try to clear things up. Here is the best link to the three blocks of the word puzzle I can find. Although some of the characters are different from what I have.  <BR> <BR>Remember, these have been put together from screen shots of a news broadcast in which the puzzle was shown for a split second. Some of the characters were completely impossible to make out. <BR> <BR><a href="http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915moa.JPG" target=_top>http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915moa.JPG</a> <BR><a href="http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915ida.JPG" target=_top>http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915ida.JPG</a> <BR><a href="http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915rusea.JPG" target=_top>http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915rusea.JPG</a> <BR> <BR>These were sent by BTK to the media.  <BR> <BR>Please don&#39;t take this the wrong way. I just think looking at the puzzle and then reading the original post in this thread will put things in perspective for you and show you the solid link between the two. <BR> <BR>My &#34;theory&#34; is that this puzzle holds much more than what has been found already. I believe each MO in the first box may coincide with one of BTKs murders, each of the IDs in box 2 could coincide with an name or ID he used etc... <BR> <BR>But the most important thing is that I believe these contain more information than what has been found. For instance there are numbers in the ID puzzle. What do these numbers mean. I can&#39;t believe they are all there for no reason, some of them may be there to throw us off but not all of them. <BR> <BR>I hope this clears up the link between the two. I also have a feeling that these are not the only word puzzles that LE / media has received from BTK. There may be one for each chapter. Now there&#39;s an idea that makes sense. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7357-->
<!--Post: 7362--><!--Time: 1108424372-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7362"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ll list the words from each section that I&#39;ve identified. We can add on from there. <BR> <BR>Also, if anyone can find significance &#40;other than what&#39;s obvious&#41; in any of these, please point it out. <BR> <BR>MO- <BR> <BR>Prowl/Fantasies/Follow/Spot/Victim/Details/Builds <BR>If odd I - Go for it &#40;this is my favorite&#41;/Cruise <BR>Sex/Plan/Five/Steam/Spy/Car/PJ <BR> <BR> <BR>ID- <BR> <BR>Gus/Telephone Co./Larry/Anderson/Officer/School <BR>Strong/WPD/Wichita/Poet <BR> <BR> <BR>Ruse- <BR> <BR>Realtor/Insurance/Serviceman/For Sale/Help Lost Dog/Wrong Address/Handyman/Remodel/Fake ID <BR> <BR>Anyone have anything else? <BR> <BR>Any ideas on the numbers? 3-1-6 / 2-6-4 / 2-6-4-3 <BR> <BR>iq <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7362-->
<!--Post: 7364--><!--Time: 1108425224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7364"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hate to keep coming back and posting additions but I had posted something in another thread and forgot to include it here.  <BR> <BR>In the middle of the ID puzzle is &#34;GEN316&#34;  <BR> <BR>Bible verse? Genesis 3:16  <BR> <BR>&#34;To the woman he said;  <BR>I will greatly increase your pains in childbearing; with pain you will give birth to children.  <BR>Your desire will be for your husband, and he will rule over you.&#34; <BR> <BR>What does everyone think? <BR> <BR>iq  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7364-->
<!--Post: 7366--><!--Time: 1108426181-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7366"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 4:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi iq, <BR> <BR>I think the 316 refers to the Wichita area code to accompany the remaining 7 digit phone number &#40;which probably goes either forward or backward judging from the way the other words are positioned, so you have 2643 or 3462&#41;. It would not be surprising to me that BTK include a double meaning with the 316 as a Biblical justification for his actions or as some form or evil sarcasm. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7366-->
<!--Post: 7368--><!--Time: 1108427566-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7368"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 4:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IQ: Yes have seen the puzzles and read your posts. Probably just a misunderstanding because of the name of the thread.  Chapter 8.MO-id ruse was on the original chapter list of May 2004, and left off of the chapter list of the Fox drop.  I understand the MO&#39;s 13 lines ID&#39;s 13 lines Ruses grid you have come up with and find it very interesting indeed. I also believe the orignal Chapter 8 MO-id ruse was a part of the chronological story of the original list and was left off of the second list possibly because BTK thought it was a mistake. So what you have found may indeed be BTK saying - &#34;this is what I meant by that&#34; which could be a cover-up.  But then, I&#39;m crazy - keep up the good posting!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7368-->
<!--Post: 7373--><!--Time: 1108432349-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7373"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 5:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Treating the numbers in the ID portion of the puzzle as a possible mixed up telephone number, here&#39;s what I got: <BR> <BR>I took it for granted that the 316 was a Wichita area code <BR>I then came up with all of the local exchanges in Wichita. I came up with 263 - 264 - 262 - 634 - 636 <BR> <BR>Then I did a reverse search of all possible numbers &#40;obviously excluding unlisted numbers&#41;. I came up with some very interesting business: <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;I am not suggesting the people associated with these business have any connection with BTK&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>First United Methodist Church Preschool <BR>330 N. Broadway 316-263-6244 <BR> <BR>Photoprose Production &#40;Commercial photography&#41;  <BR>Specializing in aircraft photography <BR>1210 W. 11th st. N. 316-262-4634 <BR> <BR>A Beauty salon <BR>A Design firm <BR>A Law firm <BR>A drilling co. <BR> <BR>There were numerous residential numbers, some interesting.  <BR> <BR>I had hoped to find an Anderson name as it is in the puzzle. Although many have VERY close numbers, none are exact. <BR> <BR>Comments? <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7373-->
<!--Post: 9670--><!--Time: 1109587714-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9670"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 2:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Now that it&#39;s an open book test: <BR> <BR>Larry Anderson = Lynn rAder roars<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9670-->
<!--Post: 10208--><!--Time: 1109816007-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10208"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 6:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How about a new way of looking at this puzzle. A third grader could have made it the way we have been interpreting it. Try doing it as a letter path, as long as your pencil follows the path, you can go any direction, up, down, across, or diagonal.  <BR> <BR>MO Grid:mull, snit, mis pig,mame, dl, dl, sit, jello, jef, leo, ciophn, six, wit, pet, hint, slit, tip, det, ht, poet, fog, your it, builds, lie, fume, jr, fox, foe, fib, nanci, then, nestle, jew,tub, tempt, toll, poll, poem, salt, hated, peot, pest, limits, sir, nanci, senor, retch, roe, ted, ten, tit, cia, dike, depth, rib, quills, unlit, slip, juke, kiss, kids, kiddo, loot, nola, jig, praise o pj, crass, flown, fib, vd, dl, sin, rat, spated, ted, dl, my four, craft, sale, hex, own, pow, two, oasis, few, im so, fall, fall, tag, stag, path, slit, pub, jails, fanci, raspy, met  <BR> <BR>ID Grid:pew, hiv, north, recoil, con, condit, shag, tear, dea, sue, ice, hones, DER son, dean, padre, step, steph, pond, sold, sob, nephew, soffi, lucy,nest, nail, dear radre, rail, rear, hero, coat, cop, read, folk, lion, front, splash, gift, shiv, fray, que, steal, fob, lean, him , her, slander,quest, snag, w&#42;ore, den, adt, dig, pray, dr, prayer, doll, dcf, VI, sos, helm, hornet, respond, wag, wage, whet, radre, con, ties, tied, tiarra, dim, boo, hoo, sue, bold, rx  <BR> <BR>Ruse Grid:leo, ceo, lane, poet, more, pore, teen, fist, fir, sister, dame, wear, dress, mace, tpm, rice, race, narc, nest, empty, slut, roar, were, camera, camera, steer, dig, ice, hope fades, six, fuse, god, shed, photo, joe, pjs, pelt, pent, fat, far, begin, sled, damn, dancer, fog, lust. leaf, toes, steal, splat, splash, knee, rein, rein, svu, oj or jo, mopes, sad, five, success, seance, cancer , reel, rest, lose, oh, rant, hark, her, ford, ruser, ask, steer, sad, grope, ode, road, rodeo, dine, dingy, post, stale, hell, hose, meet, carrot, warn, vian, nance, nam, naive, dork, bath, used, stash, seal, modas.  <BR> <BR>Well, this many words cant be a coincidence. Remember, we got fooled before because we only saw the obvious.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10208-->
<!--Post: 10426--><!--Time: 1109945757-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10426"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->One_eyed_jack<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->One_eyed_jack<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 6:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Now that we know who he is, I think it&#39;s creepy the words, Denny Lynn Rader, can individually be made from the name Larry Anderson. Did he want to get caught or was he just that full of himself?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
